          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Myosotis maritima is a species of flowering plant in the family Boraginaceae endemic to the Azores. It is found in rocks, cliffs and coastal landslides, at altitudes generally below {{convert|50|m|abbr=on}} (on the island of Flores, however, there are populations at altitudes close to {{convert|200|m|abbr=on}}). It is present in all of the islands."
          }
